#80008
"Among the Stalagmites"
"Two exceptionally large stalagmites stand here, like ancient twin columns of a
gathering-place long destroyed.  Ancient bones have drifted into the area,
collecting in random piles against stalagmites.  The stench is not so bad
here, away from the majority of the decay and rot.  The huge stalagmites block
passage east and west, forcing you to choose between going north into a
clearing, or press on south, farther into the stalagmites.
"
"[Ahni] Farther, or further? I can never remember.
Farther.  Farther is physical distance, further is metaphorical distance.  For
example, farther on down the road I will further the cause of the revolution.
