#80010
"Dead End Among the Stalagmites"
"The stalagmites here are dry and appear aged.  To the west, the stalagmites
have deep gashes in them, as if someone tried deperately to hack through
them.  The floor is littered with bits of bone and cloth, mostly gathering at
the bases of the stalagmites.  The sounds of water dripping seem far off; the
air here is stale and dry.  The only way out of this dead end is to head back
east.
"
