#80012
"Tunnel Through the Stalagmites"
"Cold, damp stone encloses the area, creating a chilly, slightly humid
atmosphere.  The ceiling is only about eight feet above the floor, and the
tunnel is not much wider.  The tunnel doesn't seem carved out, but formed over
the years over an old wooden structure.  A hole large enough for an ogre to
walk through lies to the west.  A sturdy, iron-reinforced wooden door is set
into the wall to the north.
"
