#80022
"Inside a Carved-out Dwelling"
"Crudely carved from the solid stone into a roughly eight-foot square, this
room is a simple little hovel.  A foul little bed of stained, patchworked
cloth stuffed with straw rests against the east wall.  The yellowed bones of
large humanoid creatures bound together serves as a door in the northern
wall.  The rough stone floor is covered in a considerable layer of grit,
adorned only by a worn, threadbare rug near the bed.  The southern wall is
covered by a large tapestry from which a pair of repulsive blood-red eyes seem
to watch you.
"
"[Ahni] Tapestry, move it to find stairs down.
[Ahni] 39520
